---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
const base='/equipment/16-06/', manual='https://acmerevival.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/MettlerAE100AnalyticalBalanceUserManual.pdf', utah='https://mcl.mse.utah.edu/equipment/analytical-balances/';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Mettler Toledo AE100 · tare and weigh" description="Tare an inert teaching vessel, add a known reference mass, and inspect a virtual AE100 reading and its calibration provenance." wide={true}>
<article class="equipment ae"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-06/">← Equipment 16-06</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#ae-evidence">References and verification</a></nav>
<header class="eq-mast"><span class="eq-meta">16-06 · ANALYTICAL WEIGHING / FIRST PASS</span><h2>Mettler Toledo AE100</h2><p>Tare an inert 2 g vessel, add the 5 g reference, and check that the mass displayed is 5.0000 g while the pan supports 7 g.</p></header>
<div class="grid"><section><h3>Draft-shield balance</h3><div id="ae-view" aria-label="Orbitable metric AE100 with clear sliding shield, pan, display, leveling feet and rear ports"></div><div class="bar"><button data-ae-view="overall">Reset view</button><button data-ae-view="pan">Pan and display</button><button data-ae-view="rear">Rear ports</button><button id="ae-door">Open draft shield</button></div><p id="ae-ready" role="status">Loading metric model…</p><p>Drag to orbit and pinch or scroll to zoom. The teal handle slides the right shield, and the front bar tares a valid reading.</p></section>
<section><h3>Inert tare exercise</h3><output id="ae-reading" class="readout">– – – –</output><output id="ae-detail">Nominal gross: 0 g</output><div class="fields"><label>Reference/test load (g)<input id="ae-mass" type="number" min=".00001" max="150" step="any" value="5"/></label><label>Optional seed<input id="ae-seed" type="number" min="0" max="2147483647" step="1" value="3407"/></label><label>Virtual gain error (ppm)<input id="ae-gain" type="number" min="-1000" max="1000" step="any" value="0"/></label><label class="check"><input id="ae-noise" type="checkbox"/> Enable synthetic noise</label></div>
<div class="bar"><button id="ae-example" class="primary">Run 2 g tare + 5 g reference</button><button id="ae-vessel">Load vessel</button><button id="ae-weight">Load reference/test weight</button><button id="ae-unload">Unload pan</button><button id="ae-settle">Settle and read (5 s simulated)</button><button id="ae-tare">Tare</button><button id="ae-calibrate">Ideal 100 g calibration</button><button id="ae-record">Record reading</button><button id="ae-reset">Reset</button></div>
<p id="ae-status" aria-live="polite">Run the example or open the shield to load the vessel. Then close the shield and settle before taring.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Reading record</h3><ol id="ae-log"></ol><button id="ae-export" disabled>Export readings JSON</button><p>Each saved reading includes its tare, displayed mass, gross load, display resolution, calibration ID, optional seed and modeled settling trace.</p></section>
<section id="ae-evidence"><h3>Geometry and verification</h3>
<p>Selected model: legacy 109 g AE100, clear-sided shield and manual internal calibration lever. <a href={utah}>University of Utah installed AE100 photo</a> shows the housing and single front control bar. <a href={manual+'#page=4'}>Mettler AE160/AE100 manual, printed p. 2</a> shows front/rear features and connector inventory, and <a href={manual+'#page=16'}>printed p. 14</a> supplies dimensions and specifications. Color accents and articulation distance are visual approximations.</p>
<div class="grid"><figure><img width="620" height="440" src={base+'front.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original front render of AE100 draft-glazed weighing pan, housing, and angled readout"/><figcaption>Original front render, not a hardware photograph. Compared with Utah and manual cover for enclosure, angled display and shield.</figcaption></figure><figure><img width="620" height="440" src={base+'rear.webp'} loading="lazy" alt="Original rear render showing leveling feet and rear connector bay"/><figcaption>Original rear render compared with manual printed p. 2. Individual port dimensions and positions are inferred.</figcaption></figure></div>
<div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Specification / check</th><th>Reference</th><th>Actual / interpretation</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Housing W × D × H and pan</td><td>205 × 410 × 290 mm; Ø80 mm stainless (manual p. 14)</td><td>Nominal GLB anchors. Connector and handle protrusions inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Chamber</td><td>172 × 155 × 220 mm (manual p. 14)</td><td>Interior proportions anchored; individual rails and handles inferred.</td></tr>
<tr><td>AE100 gross capacity and display increment</td><td>109 g and 0.1 mg (manual p. 14)</td><td>Gross limit applied before tare. Steps are 0.0001 g.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inert 2 g + 5 g acceptance</td><td>0.0000 g after tare, 5.0000 g after addition</td><td>Exact both; gross 2 g then 7 g, with noise disabled.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Gross load beyond 109 g; open shield</td><td>Overload despite tare / suppress stable result</td><td>Both reject, even when nominal net mass would fit.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The virtual balance computes gross load, applies gain, averages the final three synthetic signals and subtracts the saved gross estimate. It rounds to the nearest 0.0001 g, ties away from zero. Closing the shield and choosing Settle computes six points from simulated t = 0–5 s, with a diminishing transient and optional reproducible noise. The teaching stability gate is ≤0.18 mg span over the final three points, not a manufacturer algorithm. The one-point 100 g reference cancels a known synthetic gain on an empty stable pan. No measured accuracy, traceable calibration, air-buoyancy correction, environmental dynamics or weighing of actual specimens is claimed.</p>
<p><a href={base+'model.py'} download>Editable Blender generator</a> · <a href={base+'ae100.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={base+'verification.json'}>Verification</a> · <a href={base+'reference-cases.json'}>Locked reference cases</a> · <a href={base+'example-readings.json'}>Output contract example</a> · <a href={base+'xr-manifest.json'}>VR action contract</a>. No physical headset or downstream reader has been verified.</p></section>
</article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-06/browser.mjs';</script>
<style>
.ae{max-width:76rem}.ae .grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1.1rem}.ae section{border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem 0;margin:.8rem 0;min-width:0}.ae .bar{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.43rem;margin:.58rem 0}.ae .fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.52rem}.ae label{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:.18em;font-size:.91rem}.ae .check{flex-direction:row;align-items:center}.ae button,.ae input{font:inherit;color:var(--text);background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:.14rem;max-width:100%;min-width:0;min-height:2.4em;padding:.32em .52em}.ae button{cursor:pointer}.ae button:disabled{opacity:.52;cursor:default}.ae .primary{color:white;background:#245350}.ae #ae-view{height:clamp(270px,31vw,440px);background:#d9dddf;touch-action:none}.ae #ae-view :global(canvas){width:100%;height:100%;display:block}.ae .readout{display:block;padding:.25em .4em;background:#142b2e;color:#abf9c9;font:1.7rem monospace}.ae #ae-detail{display:block;white-space:pre-line;margin:.5rem 0;font:1rem monospace}.ae #ae-status.error{color:#a54a34}.ae .scroll{overflow:auto}.ae table{border-collapse:collapse;font-size:.89rem}.ae td,.ae th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);text-align:left;padding:.45rem}.ae figure{margin:.8rem 0}.ae img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:800px){.ae .grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
